  "dimensionality_fairness_note": {
    "bertopic_vec_size_hard_soft": 283,
    "lda_vec_size": 50,
    "classifier_input_dim_added_by_topic_arm": 7,
    "note": "Soft BERTopic's underlying table has 283 rows (num topics + 1 OOV slot) vs. LDA's 50 rows (K=50) - a large difference in TopicFeatureLayer's PARAMETER COUNT (283x7=1981 vs. 50x7=350). However, the actual FEATURE DIMENSION appended to the SBERT embedding before the final MLP is exactly 7 (NUM_NARRATIVES) for every one of hard/soft/lda, because TopicFeatureLayer always projects the (possibly much larger) input distribution down to a 7-dim vector via `dense_vec @ table` (a weighted sum over the table's rows) before concatenation. So the classifier itself sees the SAME input dimensionality (sbert_dim + 7) for hard/soft/lda - no variant gets an unfair advantage merely from having a larger raw feature-vector count; only the number of LEARNABLE embedding-table parameters differs, which is an inherent property of the topic model's own vocabulary size (283 BERTopic topics vs. 50 LDA topics), not an experimental design choice."
  },
